Use CSS with the `:hover` pseudo-class. The simplest way is to style the `span` normally, then change its `color` on hover.[5][6]

```html
<span class="hover-text">Hover over me</span>
```

```css
.hover-text {
  color: black;
}

.hover-text:hover {
  color: red;
}
```

If you want the color change to apply only to the text inside the `span`, `color` is the right property.[3][5]

If the `span` already has inline styles, those may override your CSS, so remove the inline styling or increase specificity if needed.[1]

